## Git and delegation

- No push blockers on the main branch, mandatory branches or worktrees, or pre-commit/pre-push hooks unless the team asks for them. Lint, types, tests and build are explicit checks.
- Delegate only when context isolation, specialization or independent parallel work pays for the coordination. Each delegated task gets an objective, minimal context, allowed files, acceptance criteria and checks. One writer per file; parallel reviewers only read.
- Check the diff and the checks before accepting delegated work.

